23:T710,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I find the owner’s name from a number plate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Owner details are not available through this tool and are protected. Use the official Vahan or Parivahan services within the permitted limits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do the letters after the RTO number mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They are the series letters. When a series reaches 9999 for an RTO, the next series letters are issued."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a BH series plate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A Bharat series plate lets eligible people keep one registration number across India when they move between states."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does a plate show a different state from the seller’s city?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The vehicle may have been bought or registered elsewhere. Ask for the NOC and confirm it has been re-registered where required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get vehicle owner details from the number plate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Owner details require the official Vahan portal. Our decoder only identifies state and RTO code from the plate format."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the Plate Decoder free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}24:T79b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use Plate Decoder","description":"Indian vehicle number plates carry useful information: the state, the RTO that registered the vehicle and a series number. This decoder reads a registration number and tells you the state and RTO code, and recognises Bharat (BH) series plates. It is helpful when you are buying a used vehicle, checki","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/vehicle-plate-decoder","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"Plate Decoder"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the plate decoder","text":"Type the registration number with or without spaces, for example DL3CAB1234 or MH12AB1234. The tool splits it into state, RTO, series and number and shows the state and the registering office where known."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"How to read an Indian number plate","text":"A standard plate follows the pattern SS NN XX NNNN. SS is the two-letter state or union territory code (DL, MH, KA, TN), NN is the two-digit RTO or district code, XX is a one-to-three-letter series, and the last four digits are the unique number."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"BH series and other special plates","text":"The Bharat series uses the format YY BH NNNN XX, where YY is the year of initial registration, BH marks the series, NNNN is a four-digit number and XX is one or two letters. It is meant for people who relocate across states often so they do not need to re-register."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Checking a used vehicle safely","text":"Decoding the plate tells you where the vehicle was first registered, which is only one clue. Before buying, verify the RC, check for pending challans, confirm the insurance and verify the chassis and engine numbers against the documents. If the registration state differs from the seller’s city, ask about the NOC and re-registration status."}]}19:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Plate Decoder\",\"alternateName\":\"Vehicle Number Plate Decoder — RTO & State India\",\"description\":\"Decode Indian vehicle registration numbers to identify state, RTO code, and BH Bharat series plates.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/vehicle-plate-decoder\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to use the plate decoder, How to read an Indian number plate, BH series and other special plates, Checking a used vehicle safely\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$23"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Plate Decoder\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/vehicle-plate-decoder\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$24"}}]],"$L25"]
